          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/924f4c4ac78b0cd3b917c694f42c0651a6f3003a"
        }
      ],
      "message": "depends: fix non-atomic reads in capnp debug assertions\n\nKJ's debug assertions read the mutex futex word and `AtomicRefcounted`\nrefcounts non-atomically. The TSan job builds capnp without optimization,\nwhich automatically enables these assertions, and TSan reports these reads\nas data races the moment KJ objects start communicating across threads.\n\nlibmultiprocess enables cross-thread communication for the first time\nin https://github.com/bitcoin-core/libmultiprocess/pull/376, which replaces\nthe pipe used in `EventLoop::sync()` with `kj::Executor::executeSync()`.\n\nPatches are the upstream commits\nhttps://github.com/capnproto/capnproto/commit/b91a6ba7c7 and\nhttps://github.com/capnproto/capnproto/commit/cc13c8c45f, which are backports\nof the v2 fixes in capnproto/capnproto#2781 and capnproto/capnproto#2843\n(https://github.com/capnproto/capnproto/pull/2855).",
